  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'gastronomic tourism' has become increasingly popular in recent years. It refers to the practice of traveling to a specific region or country with the primary intention of experiencing and enjoying its local cuisine. This trend is driven by several factors, including the desire for authenticity and the need for unique experiences.\n\nOne of the key aspects of gastronomic tourism is the emphasis on traditional cooking methods and ingredients. Visitors are often eager to learn about the history and cultural significance behind specific dishes, as well as the techniques used in their preparation. This can lead to a deeper appreciation and understanding of the local culture, beyond just the food itself.\n\nHowever, critics argue that this trend has also led to the commercialization of traditional cuisine, with some restaurants catering specifically to tourists' expectations rather than preserving authentic recipes. This raises questions about the impact of gastronomic tourism on local communities and the preservation of cultural heritage.\n\nAs a result, it is essential for travelers to be mindful of their actions and to respect local customs and traditions when engaging in gastronomic activities. By doing so, they can contribute positively to the local economy while also preserving the authenticity of the culinary experience.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the primary intention of tourists who engage in gastronomic tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To learn about traditional cooking methods\", \"To visit famous landmarks\", \"To experience and enjoy local cuisine\", \"To take part in cultural festivals\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To experience and enjoy local cuisine\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is a key aspect of gastronomic tourism, according to the text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The emphasis on modern cooking methods\", \"The desire for unique experiences\", \"The focus on traditional ingredients\", \"The need for authenticity\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The need for authenticity\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is a potential consequence of gastronomic tourism, according to the text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The preservation of cultural heritage\", \"The commercialization of traditional cuisine\", \"The decline of local restaurants\", \"The increase in food prices\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The commercialization of traditional cuisine\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What does the author suggest that travelers should be mindful of when engaging in gastronomic activities?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Their own culinary preferences\", \"Local customs and traditions\", \"The impact on local communities\", \"The cost of food\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Local customs and traditions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards gastronomic tourism, as inferred from the text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It is a positive trend that promotes cultural exchange\", \"It has both positive and negative effects on local communities\", \"It is a threat to traditional cuisine and culture\", \"It is a necessary evil for economic growth\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It has both positive and negative effects on local communities\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
